 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "미래 표현 모아 보기: will / going to / present continuous / would like to",
   "en": "future forms review: will, going to, present continuous and would like to"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "미래를 말하는 방법은 여러 가지입니다. be going to는 이미 정한 계획, will은 즉흥적인 결정이나 약속, 현재진행형(I'm meeting a friend)은 확정된 약속, would like to는 소망을 나타냅니다. 하나의 대화에서 알맞게 섞어 쓰는 것이 중요합니다.",
   "en": "There are several ways to talk about the future. Use be going to for decided plans, will for quick decisions and promises, the present continuous for fixed arrangements and would like to for wishes. A natural conversation mixes them."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "be going to",
     "I'm going to move to Paris."
    ],
    [
     "will",
     "I'll save money."
    ],
    [
     "현재진행 / arrangement",
     "I'm meeting a friend at 3 tomorrow."
    ],
    [
     "would like to",
     "One day I'd like to be a writer."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "정한 계획 = going to, 즉흥 = will.",
    "en": "Decided plan = going to; quick decision = will."
   },
   {
    "ko": "확정된 약속은 현재진행형.",
    "en": "Fixed arrangement: present continuous."
   },
   {
    "ko": "소망은 would like to.",
    "en": "A wish: would like to."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
